---
title: Cellular automata
---
Random noise, with cell life rules applied to every tile again and again, until a natural-looking map comes out of it [[t:73-74 t:83-84 s:9]].

## The rule
1. **Noise:** every tile, the map’s edge included, starts as wall with a set chance, else as floor. The demo: 55% [[c03:19-29]].
2. **Repeat 10 times,** for every tile inside the map’s outer ring at once [[c03:31-34 c03:56-70]]:
   1. count the walls among the tile’s 8 neighbors, in a copy of the map made before the pass [[c03:40-60]];
   2. 0 walls: the tile becomes wall [[c03:61-66]];
   3. 1 to 4 walls: the tile becomes floor [[c03:61-66]];
   4. 5 or more walls: the tile becomes wall [[c03:61-66]].

@@diagram cellular-count alt="Three tiles, each with its eight neighbors, before a pass and after it. The first has no wall among its neighbors and becomes wall. The second has two and becomes floor. The third has five and becomes wall." caption="A tile’s count of walls among its 8 neighbors (top) decides what it becomes (bottom): 0, wall; 1 to 4, floor; 5 or more, wall. Only the middle tile’s change is drawn." key="0:count 2:count 5:count"
..._..#_##.
.0._.2#_#5.
..._..._##.
___________
..._..#_##.
.W._.F#_#W.
..._..._##.

- **Talk says:** no neighbors, a wall; 1 to 4, empty; 5 or more, a wall [[t:80-82]].
- **Demo:** the neighbors it counts are walls, and a tile’s own state plays no part in what it becomes [[c03:40-70]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=1

## Controls
@@control wall_percent
Chance each tile starts as wall [[c03:19-29]].
@@control iterations
Times the rule is applied to the whole map [[c03:31-34 c03:56-70]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

- **Talk says:** it can give you chunks of the map that you can’t get to [[t:222-223]].
- **Cellular automata:** {{c03.regions.median}} regions at the median; never fewer than {{c03.regions.min}} [[run:c03.regions.median c03.regions.min]].
  - **Why:** the rule says nothing about joining the caves up [[own]].
- **Path:** the map has no start and exit of its own, so it is measured between [our probe’s](#our-definitions) two points. On {{c03.path.nulls}} of 200 seeds they lie in different caves [[run:c03.path.nulls]].

